    "result_text": "Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers postcode over city. Changes were kept to two files with small, cohesive additions:\n\n**`Locality.java`** \u2014 added a postcode-first overload alongside the existing city-only method (which is untouched):\n- `of(String city, String postcode)` \u2014 resolves the region from the postcode range first, falling back to the existing city-to-region table.\n- `regionForPostcode(String)` \u2014 a small private helper mapping a 4-digit postcode to NSW (2000\u20132099), VIC (3000\u20133099), or QLD (4000\u20134099), returning `null` when absent or out of range so the city fallback kicks in.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping expression now passes `owner.getPostcode()` in addition to `owner.getCity()`.\n\nStructural impact stayed low: the existing `of(String)` and `RequirePostcode` are unchanged, all new logic lives in small methods within the tiny `Locality` class (low WMC_other), and the mapper edit is a single expression line. Known cities with an in-range postcode still resolve to the same region, while a city sharing a name is now disambiguated by its postcode \u2014 e.g. an unknown city with postcode `3000` correctly yields `VIC`.",
