    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered chain of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, traced from `owners.POST.yml` through each function class.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. The whole endpoint requires the `OWNER_ADMIN` role; otherwise it never reaches step 1.\n\n## Pipeline steps (in order)\n\n**1. `RequireOwnerFields`** (reads `@RequestBody`, publishes the body for later steps)\n- *Side-effect:* normalises `address` in place via `NormaliseAddress` \u2014 trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`); null/blank becomes `\"\"`.\n- *Validation:* `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (lists all missing fields).\n- *Side-effect + validation:* converts `telephone` to E.164 via `E164Telephone` (strips spaces/dashes/brackets, defaults country code `+61` dropping a leading `0`, enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length); if it can't form a valid number \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"telephone\")`. On success the normalised telephone is written back in place.\n\n**2. `RequirePostcode`** (reads the published body)\n- *Validation:* `postcode` is optional. If present it must be exactly 4 digits; and if the **city** maps to a known region (`Locality.of(city)` \u2192 NSW/VIC/QLD \u2014 note this keys off the city name, *not* the postcode) the value must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode is skipped.\n\n**3. `NormaliseEmail`**\n- *Validation:* `email` is optional; if present it must match a basic email regex \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException(\"email\")`.\n- *Side-effect:* lower-cases `email` in place. Absent email skipped.\n\n**4. `RequireUniqueIdentity`** *(transaction governance begins here)*\n- *Validation:* loads all owners and rejects with `DuplicateTelephoneException` if any existing owner has the same (already-normalised) `telephone`.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f Note: the class comment describes an `IdentityKey`-based check, but the code as written compares the telephone string only.\n\n**5. `RequireCityCapacity`**\n- *Validation:* counts existing owners whose `city` matches exactly; if `>= 50` (`CAPACITY`) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n**6. `RequireDailyCapacity`**\n- *Validation:* computes `day = BusinessDay.roll(registrationDate ?? today)` (weekend rolls forward to Monday), counts existing owners with that `registrationDate`; if `>= 100` (`DAILY_LIMIT`) \u2192 `DailyLimitException`.\n\n**7. `BuildOwner`**\n- *Side-effect:* maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`, then sets `registrationDate = BusinessDay.roll(registrationDate ?? today)`. Publishes the entity.\n\n**8. `AssignCustomerCode`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode` to `\"<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<seq4>\"` \u2014 first 3 chars of city and last name, upper-cased, with a 4-digit sequence = (count of owners in the same city) + 1.\n\n**9. `CountNamesakes`**\n- *Side-effect:* counts existing owners sharing the same first+last name (trimmed, case-insensitive) and stores it in `namesakeCount`.\n\n**10. `SaveOwner`**\n- *Side-effect:* persists via `ownerRepository.save(owner)`, then writes an `AUDIT` log line (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\n**11. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n- *Side-effect:* maps the saved owner to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` = (owners registered today `> 80`, via `BulkSignup`), and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nSteps 4\u201311 all carry `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the reads and the write share one transaction that commits once at the end of the pipeline.\n\nAny of the thrown exceptions is turned into an HTTP error by the matching handler under `officefloor/escalation/` (e.g. `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, `InvalidPostcodeException`, `DuplicateTelephoneException`, `CityAtCapacityException`, `DailyLimitException`)."
